---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { EGGS } from '../data/eggs.js';
// Fonts the 3D shelf paints onto its labels, poster and VCR display. Only this page loads them.
import '@fontsource/vt323/latin-400.css';
import '@fontsource/permanent-marker/latin-400.css';
import '@fontsource/sacramento/latin-400.css';
import '@fontsource/ibm-plex-mono/latin-600.css';
---
<Page id="making-of" heading="Making Of" facts={[
  ['Pages', 'Astro, static HTML'],
  ['Hosting', 'Cloudflare Pages'],
  ['First version', 'three.js, GLSL, Canvas 2D'],
]}>
  <Fragment slot="lede">
    <p>
      This site is plain static pages set on a Swiss grid. It started as something much louder: a 3D
      entertainment center where every section was a VHS tape you put in a VCR. That version still
      runs below.
    </p>
  </Fragment>

  <section class="sec">
    <h2>The shelf</h2>
    <figure class="shelf-fig" data-shelf>
      <div class="shelf-stage">
        <canvas aria-label="3D model of an entertainment center with VHS tapes, a TV, a VCR and personal objects on the shelves"></canvas>
        <p class="shelf-cue">Loading the shelf</p>
      </div>
      <p class="shelf-note" aria-live="polite">Click a tape to open its page, or anything on the side shelves to read its note.</p>
      <div class="shelf-keys" role="group" aria-label="Objects on the side shelves">
        {EGGS.map((egg, i) => egg.note && <button type="button" data-egg={i} aria-pressed="false">{egg.label}</button>)}
      </div>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="sec">
    <h2>Modeled in code</h2>
    <div class="sec-body">
      <p>
        There are no model files. The unit, the TV and the VCR are boxes and rounded boxes. The shoes are
        lofted from cross-sections written out by hand, the straw hat is a profile spun around an axis,
        and the controller is an outline extruded and beveled. Laces and cords are tubes run along curves.
      </p>
      <p>
        Almost nothing is an image either. The tape labels, the wood grain, the neon sign, the poster and
        the VCR's display are painted onto 2D canvases when the page loads, then used as textures. The one
        photograph is the polaroid. The CRT is a small GLSL shader that bulges the picture, splits the
        color channels by a hair and draws scanlines; the VCR's clock shows your local time.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec">
    <h2>Why it changed</h2>
    <div class="sec-body">
      <p>
        The shelf was fun to build and slow to use. Every page sat behind an animation, the text had to
        compete with a room full of props, and on a phone the shelf was small and the buttons were
        crowded. The work is the point, so the site now leads with it: a name, a list of projects, and
        pages you can read and link to. The shelf moved here, where it is the thing being shown.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec">
    <h2>How it's built</h2>
    <div class="sec-body">
      <ol class="flow" aria-label="How the site is built">
        <li><strong>Astro</strong><span>Every page is static HTML with its own address and link preview</span></li>
        <li><strong>One grid</strong><span>Twelve columns, one typeface, one accent color</span></li>
        <li><strong>View transitions</strong><span>A project's name grows into its page title</span></li>
        <li><strong>Pages Function</strong><span>One small server route asks Spotify what I'm playing</span></li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        The footer's "now playing" line comes from a Cloudflare Pages Function that asks Spotify with a refresh
        token it keeps as a secret, and caches the answer for 30 seconds. The link-preview images are drawn
        in code at build time from the same list of pages the site is built from.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Page>

<script>
  import '../scripts/shelf.js';
</script>
